# Agent personas
Keep this file extensionless so it is not loaded as a persona.

Markdown bodies append instructions; optional frontmatter shares the agent execution
options used by cron, channels, and webhook transforms:

- model: provider:modelId
- reasoningEffort: the shared Pi thinking level
- allowedTools: bus-method glob whitelist; built-in Pi tools are unaffected
- skills: discovered skill-name glob whitelist (not paths or skill execution)

Omit fields to keep existing defaults. Empty tool/skill lists inherit the persona
or normal discovery. Use commented examples rather than bare YAML keys (null).
Explicit execution options override persona options. Model/reasoning can change
on a running session; tool/skill selections apply when the session is created.
Changing those selections requires a new session; automatic rotation retains them.

Channel personas are seeded from default.md; subagents use subagent.md.
Cron and webhooks pass their own options without acquiring a channel persona.
Voice uses voice.md for instructions, bus tools, and available skills. Its live
speech model remains configured in settings.json voice.provider/voice.model;
background agent.execute calls use the shared options and default to low reasoning.

Bundled templates are copied only when missing; existing user files are preserved.
